@startuml AD-7_fault_and_alert
!include _style.iuml
title AD-7 (WF-04) Pillar Fault: Report, Alert and Remote Recovery\n<size:11>Scope: PowerMe «software system» · Trigger: driver report, pillar fault or pillar silent · Owner: Trần Trọng Nghĩa · v2.1</size>

|PowerMe Platform\n«software system»|
|Operator\n«person»|
|#EEEEEE|Charging Pillar\n«external system»|
|PowerMe Platform\n«software system»|
start
:Receive fault signal; <<input>>
switch ( )
case ([driver reported a faulty\npillar (UC-CHG-05)])
  :Record driver's fault report;
case ([pillar reported a connector\nFaulted (UC-INT-04)])
  :Connector\n[Faulted]; <<task>>
  if ( ) then ([session running on it])
    :Close session with fault reason\nand bill energy delivered (AD-1);
  else ([else])
  endif
case ([pillar silent for 900 s])
  :ChargingPillar\n[offline] (AD-2); <<task>>
endswitch
:Hide connector from search\nand suggestions;
:FaultEvent\n[raised]; <<task>>
:Raise fault alert (≤ 900 s offline); <<output>>
|Operator\n«person»|
:Receive and acknowledge alert\n(UC-OPS-03); <<input>>
|PowerMe Platform\n«software system»|
:FaultEvent\n[acknowledged]; <<task>>
|Operator\n«person»|
if ( ) then ([remote reset may fix it])
  :Send remote reset\n(UC-OPS-04);
  |PowerMe Platform\n«software system»|
  if ( ) then ([a driver is charging on\nanother connector])
    :Warn: reset restarts the whole pillar; <<output>>
    |Operator\n«person»|
    :Confirm the reset a second time;
    |PowerMe Platform\n«software system»|
  else ([else])
  endif
  :FaultEvent\n[resetting]; <<task>>
  :Send reset command; <<output>>
  |#EEEEEE|Charging Pillar\n«external system»|
  :Restart and report status;
  |PowerMe Platform\n«software system»|
  if ( ) then ([connector works again: Available,\nPreparing, Charging, …])
    :Connector\n[working]; <<task>>
    :Show connector in search again;
    :FaultEvent\n[resolved]; <<task>>
    stop
  else ([reset refused, timeout\nor still Faulted])
    :FaultEvent\n[acknowledged]; <<task>>
  endif
else ([needs site visit])
endif
|Operator\n«person»|
:Fix on site, then close alert;
|PowerMe Platform\n«software system»|
:FaultEvent\n[resolved]; <<task>>
stop
note right
  Maintenance tickets are Should (FR-18),
  not part of WF-04.
  v2.1 (28/10/2026, PR #61 review): a fault
  closes on any working status, not only
  Available; reset asks twice when another
  connector is charging. Unavailable during
  the reboot does not close the fault.
end note
!include _legend.iuml
@enduml